# 11. AUTOMATION SIMULATION ENGINE

This is one of the most important modules.

Implement a real internal simulation engine.

Do not make routines merely decorative cards.

The engine should:

1. Receive a simulated event.
2. Identify matching routines.
3. Evaluate trigger conditions.
4. Check exceptions.
5. Check routine priorities.
6. Detect possible conflicts.
7. Determine the resulting actions.
8. Update application state.
9. Generate activity logs.
10. Display the execution result.

## Conflict handling

When multiple routines match:

- Evaluate their conditions.
- Use routine priority.
- Detect conflicting actions.
- Avoid executing contradictory actions blindly.
- Explain which routine was selected and why.

If a conflict cannot be resolved safely, request user confirmation.

## Simulation controls

Create a dedicated way to test automation.

Let the user simulate:

- Current time.
- Day of week.
- Entering a location.
- Leaving a location.
- Starting an activity.
- Incoming call.
- Incoming message.

Show:

- Trigger received.
- Matching routines.
- Conditions evaluated.
- Exceptions checked.
- Actions selected.
- Final simulated result.

The simulation engine must use the same application state as the rest of the app.

